> Topic: Contributions
> (essay time!)
> 1. Which class do you think is the easiest to play, and why?

Samurai: Early game they hit the hardest in melee.  Late game they
still hit the hardest in melee.  A samurai using +7 yumi and +7 ya (at
expert) does more damage than a ranger using +7 longbow of diana and +7
arrows (at expert).  If you max stats and level, they're obscenely
effective offensive spellcasters (almost as good as knights and
wizards)

> 2. Consider the choice of genociding spellcasters versus powerful melee
> monsters.

I've been playing genoless lately.  Only (master) mind flayers and
certain named monsters still scare me.

> 3. Evaluate the usefulness of chaotic artifacts.

None of them are useless:

Stormbringer: is one of the better (melee) artifact weapons
[IMO only Grayswandir,  Snickersnee, and Excalibur (in that order) are
all-around better].
Longbow of Diana: near-unlimited ammo is nice ... especially when
poisoned +7
MKoT: Who is going to argue with half-damage?
Orcrist/Sting: they have their uses
Grimtooth: never found it, never used it, don't have an opinion.

